{"ts_utc": "2026-05-13T11:37:25.994267Z", "run_id": "20260513_113712_rag_L3_S_I3_1f65c6", "seq": 5, "event": "generation.completed", "payload": {"answer": "Parliament did not explicitly state its position on education policy. However, it was mentioned that the Free Senior High School (FSHS) Programme has been a flagship initiative of the previous Government [09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856:52]. \n\nParliament also discussed the challenges faced by parents due to the computer school placement, which was released on Tuesday, 28th November [dfb854d2e036ec0d7e95b53e94c88bfc469f0184a4bc76853bf8d865ecd5540c:74]. \n\nA Member of Parliament mentioned that basic education should be compulsory for every child of school-going age, but the focus on SHS level has further exacerbated the deterioration of quality education in the country [2fc50d4e2a88b6bf595eef06a7e0ea916fc876c9f0060a7868a860ee4fe7bf99:22].", "answer_sha256": "306b0cd3f802006b5f7fc786d414d06575ed4308313ac6fb075cf71c72345df4"}, "prev_hash": "d70cbb0be6dd52038c64072f7af780c834d0ef298ffbf8f888c9357689fb47dc", "event_hash": "14b298a7959aeb0a6723cee7a4c87e8f6468196b93f4800d83079222dd778eca"}
